    "id": "2011260468975771862",
    "author": "iamtrebuh",
    "quote": "My AI setup as a solo founder\n\nbuilt it with @openclaw, here's how it works:\n\n4 agents, each with their own job:\n\n- main one: strategy, planning, big picture. coordinates the others\n- dev agent: coding, technical problems, architecture decisions\n- marketing agent: research, content ideas, competitor analysis\n- business agent: pricing, metrics, growth strategy\n\nwhat makes it actually useful:\n\n- shared memory for the big stuff (project docs, goals, key decisions)\n- but each agent also has their own context (past messages)\n- different models for different jobs (codex for coding, Gemini for marketing etc)\n- scheduled daily tasks without me asking (content prompts, reddit monitoring, reminders)\n- agents can work in parallel\n- connected to my notes so nothing gets lost\n\nIt all runs on my VPS and I control them all through Telegram, so it basically works as a real small team available 24/7. I even gave them names and different characters:\n- Milo (leader - confident and charismatic),\n- Josh (business guy - pragmatic and straight to the point, numbers-driven),\n- Angela (marketing - extroverted, funny and full of ideas),\n- Bob (coding - introverted analytical genius).\n\nI'm still setting up all the skills, but so far it really works great and it's a first use case that's so beneficial to me and can help me in my daily work.",
